      "body": "## What\r\n\r\nRestore the ROCm/aiter#6042 patch that #44534 removed. The patch is now applied from its squash-merge commit `57e2c6b42` on AITER main instead of the PR-branch commit `042a28918`.\r\n\r\n## Why\r\n\r\n#44534 dropped the cherry-pick because it assumed the `2bb549102` pin already contains ROCm/aiter#6042. It doesn't: the pin is from Oct 10 and ROCm/aiter#6042 merged on Oct 13. The old cherry-pick conflicted because ROCm/aiter#6159 rewrote `pa_decode_sparse.py` between the previous pin and this one. `042a28918` was written before that rewrite, while the squash-merge commit was made after it.\r\n\r\nWithout the patch, the gfx950 sparse MLA decode on 64-bit gathers uses the peeled kernel, which spills about 110 VGPRs below Triton 3.8. That affects the ROCm 7.2 / 7.2.4 images (Triton 3.7.0). The ROCm 10 images run Triton 3.8.0, so the patch doesn't change their behavior.\r\n\r\nROCm/aiter#5967 and ROCm/aiter#6007 are in the pin, so their patches stay removed.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n- Checked out `2bb549102` in a local AITER clone and ran `git cherry-pick --no-commit 57e2c6b42`. It applies cleanly, and the result matches `pa_decode_sparse.py` at `57e2c6b42` exactly.\r\n- `release-docker-amd-rocm720-nightly.yml` built from this change, all four flavors (gfx942/gfx950 x rocm720/rocm724): https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38803779443. The cherry-pick applied in all four builds and the images built.\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "michaelzhang-ai"
            },
            "body": "Closing, per @1am9trash:\r\n\r\n> This shouldn't be needed. New perf move to ROCm 10, so ROCm 7.2 only needs to run correctly. Otherwise we keep piling patches into the Docker image.\r\n\r\nThe ROCm 10 images ship Triton 3.8 and don't need this patch. ROCm/aiter#6042 will come in with the next AITER pin bump.\r\n",
